Sunday
Today we had sacrament meeting, priest quorum, =E2=80=9Cgo and do=E2=80=9D,=
 a devotional,
and a special hour or so of some dude singing and playing the guitar (his
last name was Deere, I can remember that much). It was a pretty busy day,
and I was still pretty congested but I made it through it.

Monday
Today we had our last HOA which was a little emotional for me (pretty sure
my companion could care less about being done =F0=9F=98=82); I am very appr=
eciative
for everything that Izumi-san has helped us learn, regardless of If she's
feigning not knowing about the church. We had an alright but pretty stale
class with our first new instructor, and later we had Class with our other
new teacher, which I think was a little more energetic at least.

Tuesday
Today I also went to the clinic to get prescribed some medicine, and me and
my companion got to walk a block or two to a pharmacy for some. Afterwards
we had one run of the mill afternoon class, but our Evening Devotional was
with Elder Gong which was awesome. I totally forgot how much he loved
telling dad jokes and I feel like I really connected over that =F0=9F=98=82=
 He spoke
a lot about not just being obedient but being eagerly obedient; obeying
commandments out of a desire, not just because we've been asked to.

Wednesday
On Wednesday we had the regular 7 hours of class, within which we practiced
promising blessings for keeping and making commitment. We also filled out a
bunch of surveys since we're almost at the end of our MTC stay. I also did
a little drawing so I'll attach a few photos.

Thursday we had the cafeteria shift, which I was absolutely vibing with,
although That was probably not the popular opinion among my district lol.
While we were behind the scenes preparing food I also saw some stairs
leading into the ground; Pretty sure they have a dungeon back there =F0=9F=
=91=80
Pretty much all of the latter end of this week we've been making paper
cranes so I'll attach a few pictures.

Friday we had a pretty normal two classes, but we said our last official
goodbyes to Brother Marks. He gave us each a signed mission card from his
mission, and we all got to sign a big Japanese flag that he had. In classes
we are mostly just reviewing Stuff at this point, but we talked about
mostly how to teach according to someone's needs rather than just a lesson
plan. today I also finished Alma (albeit I listened to the audio) but I'd
still like to go through and mark The stuff I really got a lot out of.

Saturday (P-Day)
Fun fact P day in Japanese is =E3=81=98=E3=82=85=E3=81=86=E3=82=93=E3=81=B3=
=E3=81=AE=E3=81=B2 which literally just means
preparation day but it is pretty fun to say lol. Today I talked with fam,
played an hour of spikeball in the very hot sun, an hour of volleyball in
the gym, and shone my shoes. Pretty run of the mill P day but I definitely
had fun, I think my shoes look pretty fun too, I've definitely been using a
lot of black on brown =F0=9F=91=9E

This will be my last email sent from America!! (For the next two ish years
at least lol) I am super ready for Japan; there's so much I don't know and
also so much that I know I won't understand, but that doesn't matter as
long as I'm doing my best, and what the Lord would be having me do.

Love you guys!!

=E3=80=8BSpiritual thought=E3=80=8A
As I've been reading through the war chapters of Alma, it's been
interesting to draw parallels between the time of the Nephites and
Lamanites. Alma 48 reads:

8 Yea, he had been strengthening the armies of the Nephites, and erecting
small forts, or places of resort; throwing up banks of earth round about to
enclose his armies, and also building walls of stone to encircle them
about, round about their cities and the borders of their lands; yea, all
round about the land.
9 And in their weakest fortifications he did place the greater number of
men; and thus he did fortify and strengthen the land which was possessed by
the Nephites.

Just as Moroni was strengthening the people where they were more weak, we
also need to especially fortify ourselves where we are more prone to
temptations or tuning out the Spirit. If you genuinely need help in an area
God will make it happen if you are doing all you can

-Elder Killian

